{"n": 586, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "586.webp", "text": "323052\n\n3032075\n\n32-11\n\nPull steering spindle out of bearing.\nRemove snap ring (1), collar ring (2)\nand ring (3).\n\nPull out steering spindle from above.\n\ninstallation;\n\nNotch of collar ring (2) must lock snap\nring (1).\n\nStem of ring (3) faces bearing.\n\nInstall snap ring with Special Tools\n323 052 and 32 3 050.\n\nHf applicable, shove steering spindle\ndown and drive out bearings.\n\nDrive In bearings with Special Tool\n00 5 550.\n\n32:31 070 REMOVING AND INSTALLING\nOR REPLACING LOWER\nSTEERING SPINDLE\n\nThe entire steering spindle should al-\nways be replaced when a coupling or\nuniversal jolt Is faulty:\n\nRemove steering wheel - see\n\n32:33 000.\n\nInstallation:\nMount steering wheel In straight ahead\nposition.\n\nRemove bolt (1) and loosen bolt (2).\nPress steering spindle off of steering\ngear and remove.\n\ndnstailation:\n\nBolt (1) must be located In the locking\ngroove of the steering shaft.\n\nReplace selfocking nuts.\n\nTightening torque*.\n\nInstafation:\n\nSteering wheel and front wheels posi-\ntioned straight ahead (marks on hous-\nIng and steering shaft aligned).\nMount steering spindle on steering\ngear In such a manner that the slot of\nthe universal joint is allgned with the\nmark on the steering gear.\n\nMake sure spring washers (1) are In-\nStalled between coupling and steering\nspindle or universal joint when as-\nsembling a new steering spindle.\nTightening torque*.\n\n* See Specifications", "words": [["323052", 0.0616, 0.4613, 0.1182, 0.4746], ["3032075", 0.2025, 0.5076, 0.249, 0.5155], ["32-11", 0.4732, 0.0324, 0.5328, 0.0562], ["Pull", 0.2803, 0.076, 0.3005, 0.0886], ["steering", 0.3045, 0.0773, 0.3485, 0.0912], ["spindle", 0.3515, 0.0773, 0.3909, 0.0912], ["out", 0.3939, 0.0773, 0.4111, 0.0886], ["of", 0.4152, 0.0773, 0.4253, 0.0886], ["bearing.", 0.4293, 0.0773, 0.4722, 0.0925], ["Remove", 0.2813, 0.0939, 0.3242, 0.1044], ["snap", 0.3283, 0.0952, 0.3535, 0.10